<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0

  Privacy manifest. Required by App Store Connect: without one, uploads draw ITMS-91053 warnings and
  the privacy report Apple generates for the listing cannot be assembled.

  All four keys are declared explicitly, including the empty ones. An absent key and an empty array
  mean the same thing to Apple's tooling but not to a reader — "we collect nothing" and "nobody filled
  this in" would otherwise be the same file.

    NSPrivacyTracking            false  no tracking of any kind.
    NSPrivacyTrackingDomains     empty  nothing to list. The only third-party dependency is swift-sodium
                                        (libsodium), used for the vault's cryptography. It makes no network
                                        requests, collects nothing, and ships no manifest of its own.

    NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes  three entries, all for OPTIONAL features:

      AudioData   The voice recording sent for analysis when the person uses voice capture. It is kept by
                  the recognition service in memory only until it is processed (at most 48 hours), then
                  discarded. Not linked to an identity, not used for tracking.
      PhotosorVideos  The meal photo sent for analysis when the person photographs a meal (camera or
                  library). Re-encoded on the phone first: no location or camera metadata, longest side
                  1024 px. Same handling as the voice recording: kept in memory only until processed (at
                  most 48 hours), then discarded. Not linked to an identity, not used for tracking.
      UserID      The username of the cloud vault account, which voice capture requires. No email is
                  asked for or stored. Linked (it is the account), not used for tracking.

                  NOT declared: the vault records, which are the voice results AND the whole meal journal
                  once a vault account is linked. They are encrypted on the phone and the server only ever
                  holds ciphertext it cannot read, and the passphrase never leaves the device. Whether Apple
                  counts that as "collected" (and as which category: the journal is food and health data)
                  is for App Store Connect's questionnaire to settle, and is the first thing to recheck; the
                  entries above are what the app transmits in a form the service can read.

      Everything else stays on the device: the food journal is a JSON file in Application Support (plus,
      with a vault account, its encrypted copy in the vault), and the nutrition requests (GET /ingredients/search, GET /ingredients/barcode, POST /nutrition) send a
      food name, a barcode number, a weight and a cooking method, with no identifier.

    NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes    two required-reason categories, each used and nothing more:

      UserDefaults    CA92.1  reads and writes the app's own preferences: language, the server addresses,
                              and a marker telling a fresh install from a relaunch.
      FileTimestamp   C617.1  RecognitionEntryStore reads the modification date of the voice recordings in
                              the app's own container to delete audio older than its retention period.

      Not declared, because not used: system boot time, disk space and active keyboard.

  Recheck this file when a feature starts sending something new off the device, or when any API in the
  required-reason list (file timestamp, boot time, disk space, keyboard, user defaults) is used somewhere
  new. Over-declaring misdescribes the app just as under-declaring does.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>

    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>

    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeAudioData</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePhotosorVideos</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeUserID</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>

    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>CA92.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>C617.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
